From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Thu, 18 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] media: rkcif: honour the mbus_code filter when enumerating
 formats

rkcif_stream_enum_formats() returns every entry of out_fmts[] regardless of
the v4l2_fmtdesc mbus_code the caller asked about, so userspace is told that
an 8-bit Bayer input can be captured as, among other things, 10-bit Bayer.

libcamera's simple pipeline handler builds its format map by enumerating the
video node once per sensor media bus code and believes the answer, so it ends
up pairing SBGGR8_1X8 on the subdev links with SGRBG10 on the video node:

  Picked 1920x1080-SBGGR8_1X8/Unset -> 1920x1080-SGRBG10
  Link 'ov5648 2-0036'[0] -> 'dw-mipi-csi2rx fdfb0000.csi'[0]:
        configured with format 1920x1080-SBGGR8_1X8/RAW

VICAP then expects 3840 bytes per line while the receiver delivers 1920, no
frame ever completes and capture hangs with the buffers queued and no error
reported anywhere. Reproduced by hand: 8-bit links with a 10-bit video format
yield nothing in 20 seconds, while the same links with BA81 give three frames
in two.

The format table already carries the matching mbus_code for every entry, so
just skip the ones that do not match.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
---
diff -ruN ef_a/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkcif/rkcif-stream.c ef_b/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkcif/rkcif-stream.c
--- a/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkcif/rkcif-stream.c	2026-09-18 11:00:05.366436200 +0200
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkcif/rkcif-stream.c	2026-09-18 11:00:05.392747182 +0200
@@ -395,13 +395,28 @@
 				     struct v4l2_fmtdesc *f)
 {
 	struct rkcif_stream *stream = video_drvdata(file);
+	unsigned int found = 0;
+	unsigned int i;
 
-	if (f->index >= stream->out_fmts_num)
-		return -EINVAL;
+	for (i = 0; i < stream->out_fmts_num; i++) {
+		const struct rkcif_output_fmt *fmt = &stream->out_fmts[i];
 
-	f->pixelformat = stream->out_fmts[f->index].fourcc;
+		/*
+		 * VICAP writes what the CSI-2 receiver hands it straight to
+		 * memory, so only the formats matching the media bus code are
+		 * usable. Honour the filter rather than advertising all of
+		 * them for every input.
+		 */
+		if (f->mbus_code && fmt->mbus_code != f->mbus_code)
+			continue;
 
-	return 0;
+		if (found++ == f->index) {
+			f->pixelformat = fmt->fourcc;
+			return 0;
+		}
+	}
+
+	return -EINVAL;
 }
 
 static int rkcif_stream_enum_framesizes(struct file *file, void *fh,
